 dict(id='S06',citation='Bennedsen, Christensen & Christensen, To be or not to be: Roughness or long memory in volatility?, arXiv2403.12653, revised author text January2026.',version='60PDF pages. Cover indicates revisions following referee input, but exact journal bibliographic mapping remains unresolved; do not call this downloaded version a published2026 article.',refs='PDFpp1-5: MCLE scope and limitations; pp6-7: composite likelihood; pp36-37: discussion; p45: moment benchmarks.',model='Stationary Gaussian fOU and generalized Cauchy dependence, with distinct short-/long-run behavior.',observation='Intraday log spot-RV proxies remain noisy; the paper explicitly notes potential estimator distortion and studies log trading volume as related evidence (p5,p37).',estimator='Composite likelihood based on low-dimensional marginal/conditional Gaussian densities; asymptotic rate and limit shape depend on memory and whether the mean is known (p3).',data='Main empirical application is cryptocurrency high-frequency data, excluded from our own empirical scope; methods may inform the equity design.',finding='The authors find decoupled short-/long-run correlation structure useful, while explicitly recognizing RV proxy limitations.',limits='Their fixed-spacing long-span framework does not validate daily OLS slope standard errors. Memory can change inference; no generic block bootstrap guarantee follows.',replication='Full text acquired; targeted methods audit only; no MCLE code or empirical result reproduced.',adds='Require separate persistence controls and assess dependence-specific inference instead of importing an off-the-shelfH interval.'),
 dict(id='S07',citation='Bennedsen, Christensen, Christensen, Yu & Zhang (2026), The Rough HAR Model, arXiv2609.21587.',version='42PDF pages; working paper/preprint. Author faculty page lists it as submitted. Published status not asserted.',refs='PDFpp12-13 eqs2.7-2.9 and footnotes5-6; pp17-18 ETF sample/forecast design; pp22-24 Table5 and explicit noise test eqs4.1-4.2. p23 visually inspected.',model='Log-RAR is ARMA(1,1); log-RHAR replaces AR1 with daily/5day/22day HAR regressors and MA1 innovation. Discrete-time roughness terminology is qualified by the authors themselves.',observation='Section4 explicitly models observed logRV=y=x+w with independent noise. The latent AR is augmented by a genuine MA1 component; fixing noise variance2/78=1/39 makes theta=0 a testable restriction (p23).',estimator='Exact Gaussian maximum likelihood via Kalman filter; simulations map MA coefficient to fGn Wold coefficient. Empirical forecast window500days, refit daily, lognormal retransformation; source QLIKE is nonnegative ratio form (p18).',data='Ten ETFs plus a40stock VOLARE robustness panel. SPY and sector ETFs, 5minute RV; exact source fields and author code not acquired.',finding='The authors report negative MA coefficients and forecast gains, with theta remaining around-0.4 under fixed measurement noise (p23). This overlaps the initial project more closely than an accuracy-only description.',limits='Known2/m error variance is an approximation; latent noise and intrinsic MA are otherwise not separable from logRV dynamics alone. A discrete ARMA path does not identify a continuous-time local Holder exponent. HARQ underperformance alone is not a general structural identification test.',replication='No RAR/RHAR estimation or source table reproduction claimed. Exact equations audited; replication code not located on inspected author pages/fulltext.',adds='Abandon the proposed novelty claim that this paper ignores measurement error. Focus on heterogeneous/correlated noise, matched covariance controls and separately measured decision sensitivity.'),
 dict(id='S08',citation='Mouti (2026), Rough Volatility Across Assets, arXiv2608.16749v1,17Aug2026.',version='29PDF pages, preprint under arXiv perpetual nonexclusive distribution license. This license does not license us to redistribute the PDF.',refs='PDFpp7-9: observation corrections and fOU mean-reversion claim; p10 Table2; pp11-13 simulation design/Table3. pp9-10 visually inspected.',model='Stationary fOU log-variance for positive kappa; fBm case at kappa0. Grid H={.05,.10,.15,.30,.50},kappa={0,.003,.010,.020,.035}; daily dispersion calibrated to SPY.',observation='Daily latent variance drives390one-minute Gaussian return increments per day. Observed log-price adds Gaussian noise std1e-4 and5e-4; multiple RV estimators and an additive-log-error correction are compared.',estimator='OLS log second moment on lags1..10 and1..40; constant-offset correction and mean-reversion adjustments. The paper separates option-implied skew estimates from realized estimates.',data='Author reports3926US equities,34CME roots and options44underlyings over2010-2025. These restricted underlying data were not accessed or independently validated.',finding='The preprint reports persistent low corrected roughness estimates and gives an all-H fOU finite-lag contamination formula. Our Brownian special-case audit agrees with its Corollary1.',limits='Full fOU simulation initialization/parameter matching and error dependence require more audit. Numerical Table2 check matched35/48 cells within the prespecified1e-4 tolerance, with maximum difference0.00494. Independent spectral-variogram and oscillatory-covariance integrations agree in checked cells. Cause remains unresolved; do not label the paper invalid or silently replace its table.',replication='Secondary preprint formula audit: results/mouti_table2_audit.csv and latest_mouti_audit.json. Not our required published-result replication; no Tables3-6 Monte Carlo replication.',adds='Treat cross-asset noise correction and mean reversion as existing work. A bounded methodological replication/extension is more defensible than claiming discovery of apparent roughness.'),
 dict(id='S09',citation='Shi, Yu & Zhang (2025), Realized Volatility Forecasting: Continuous versus Discrete Time Models, University of Macau Working Paper202537,21Oct2025.',version='43PDF pages, official working-paper endpoint successfully downloaded after original503/incomplete-response failures. Author page lists it as submitted.',refs='PDFpp6-7 fGn likelihood; pp19-20 HAR family; pp21-22 projection/retransformation; pp23-25 economic criterion/data; p22 visually inspected.',model='Continuous-time Gaussian fBm/fOU and BSS forecasting models compared with ARFIMA, HAR/HARQ and log variants.',observation='Forecasts of realized measures; HARQ explicitly uses quarticity. An explicit additional latent-logIV/proxy noise likelihood was not found in the inspected model/projection sections; a paper-wide absence claim is not made.',estimator='Time-domain and Whittle likelihoods, rolling1255day estimation, horizons1/5/21. Eq35 uses lognormal correction; forecast range filter falls back to training mean.',data='11equity ETFs,30DJIAstocks and30crypto candidates; equities from Refinitiv Tick History at5minutes,2010-2024; RTH9:30-16:00, exclude days with<50%expected5minute observations (p25). Author-linked data ZIP returned403 locally and was not accessed.',finding='Economic forecasting overlap is substantial: risky-asset weight proportional to inverse forecast volatility and a risk-parity utility proxy with Sharpe0.4,gamma2 (pp24-25). Statistical and economic rankings are explicitly separate.',limits='Printed stationary conditional variance below eq35 is gamma0+Gamma^T Sigma^-1 Gamma. Gaussian conditioning requires a MINUS; our formula notebook/tests use the minus. The printed sign was visually checked, but author code is unavailable, so no claim is made that actual numerical results used it. Their utility proxy is not a transaction-cost/cash/overnight-accounted realized strategy return.',replication='Full text acquired and targeted equations audited. Official replication archive identified but403blocks access; no market forecast table replicated.',adds='Do not claim first economic-value comparison of rough forecasts. Use aligned risk tracking, comparable observation treatment and executable accounting as a potential bounded extension.'),
